Running leader and follower arms together on desktop:
snoopy - name of leader arm
woodstock - name of follwer arm
/dev/ttyACM0 (used for follower arm)
/dev/ttyACM1 (used for leader arm)
runs teleoperate arms:
lerobot-teleoperate     --robot.type=so101_follower     --robot.port=/dev/ttyACM0     --robot.id=woodstock     --teleop.type=so101_leader     --teleop.port=/dev/ttyACM1     --teleop.id=snoopy
Helpful link in setting up arms: https://huggingface.co/docs/lerobot/en/so101?example=Linux
Note: be sure to know what port each arm is on before running the code. If it failes try switching which port is connectted to which arm. If this still fails, be sure that you have access to the port
Important: Make sure you have perms on the port

Teleoperate with real leader arm in kitchen scene on desktop:
cd Documents
cd leisaac
conda activate leisaac
rm ./datasets/dataset.hdf5 (only doing this because no data has been collected bc it keeps crashing, get new file if there is data there)
python scripts/environments/teleoperation/teleop_se3_agent.py \
  --task=LeIsaac-SO101-PickOrange-v0 \
  --teleop_device=so101leader \
  --port=/dev/ttyACM0 \
  --num_envs=1 \
  --device=cuda \
  --enable_cameras \
  --record \
  --dataset_file=./datasets/dataset.hdf5 \
  --recalibrate
Make sure you have perms for the port!!!

Resuming simulation on desktop (reinforcement learning):
ONLY WORKS ON DESSKTOP
1. Open the terminal
2. enter the the environment with: conda activate isaaclab
3. cd Documents
4. cd isaac_so_arm101
5. python scripts/rsl_rl/train.py --task SO-ARM100-Lift-Cube-v0 --num_envs 1000 --max_iterations 20000 --resume
NOTE: You must be in the environment for the command to work

Dataset collection:
ONLY WORKS ON LAPTOP (stage light --> click default)
1. log onto the laptop (check your email for the login info Akbas sent it)
2. Open the terminal
3. cd Documents
4. cd leisaac
5. conda activate isaaclab
6. Plug in the real leader arm to the computer, also plug in the power supply USE THE 5V ONE
7. be sure you have port perms, sudo chmod 666 /dev/ttyACM0
  The last string is the port you are getting access to, if using a different port change it
8. python ~/Documents/leisaac/scripts/environments/teleoperation/teleop_se3_agent.py   --task=LeIsaac-SO101-LiftCube-v0   --teleop_device=so101leader --port=/dev/ttyACM0   --num_envs=1  --device=cuda   --enable_cameras   --record   --dataset_file=./datasets/dataset.hdf5   --recalibrate --resume
9. You will then need to calibrate the leader arm, follow the instructions that it gives you
10. Important commands for dataset collection: b- start control, r- failed task, n- sucsessful task
